Now, a port of the decoding half of Python's json module: Do loads(text) turns JSON text into lists, Books, words, numbers, Yes/No and nil.
Now, Do parse(text) gives [Yes, value] or [No, message] instead of printing, so a caller can tell a JSON null from a mistake.
Next, dumps (turning a value back into JSON text) needs a way to ask what kind of value something is.
Next, \uXXXX escapes need a way to make a character from its number, and a very deep nesting stops at the 200 level limit on function calls.

Create is_space(c), give c in " \n\t\r"!

Create num_step(state, ch),
    Now, a small state machine for JSON's number rule: an optional minus, then 0 or a digit 1-9 followed by digits, then an optional point and digits, then an optional e or E with an optional sign and digits.
    Now, states: 0 start, 1 after -, 2 after a leading 0, 3 in the whole part, 4 after the point, 5 in the fraction, 6 after e, 7 after the sign of the exponent, 8 in the exponent.
    if state is -1, give -1.
    A digit holds ch in "0123456789".
    if state is 0 and ch is "-", give 1.
    if state is 0 and ch is "0", give 2.
    if state is 0 and digit and ch is not "0", give 3.
    if state is 1 and ch is "0", give 2.
    if state is 1 and digit and ch is not "0", give 3.
    if state is 3 and digit, give 3.
    if (state is 2 or state is 3) and ch is ".", give 4.
    if state is 4 and digit, give 5.
    if state is 5 and digit, give 5.
    if (state is 2 or state is 3 or state is 5) and (ch is "e" or ch is "E"), give 6.
    if state is 6 and (ch is "+" or ch is "-"), give 7.
    if (state is 6 or state is 7) and digit, give 8.
    if state is 8 and digit, give 8.
    give -1!

Create is_json_number(raw),
    A state holds 0.
    for every ch in raw, state holds Do num_step(state, ch).
    if state is 2 or state is 3 or state is 5 or state is 8, give Yes.
    give No!

template Parser(text),
    A text holds text.
    A pos holds 0.
    A problem holds "".
    A buf holds "".
    A ended holds No.

    Create fail(message),
        Now, only the first mistake is kept, since the later ones are just fallout from it.
        if problem is "", problem holds "{message} at position {pos}".
        give nil!

    Create skip(),
        for every step in range(Counted(text) - pos), if pos is smaller-than Counted(text) and Do is_space(text:pos), pos holds pos + 1.
        give nil!

    Create expect(ch),
        Do skip() on self.
        if pos is smaller-than Counted(text) and text:pos is ch, pos holds pos + 1, give nil.
        give Do fail("expected {ch}") on self!

    Create separator(closing),
        Do skip() on self.
        if pos is Counted(text), give Do fail("unexpected end of text") on self.
        A c holds text:pos.
        if c is ",", pos holds pos + 1, give ",".
        if c is closing, pos holds pos + 1, give closing.
        give Do fail("expected a comma or {closing}") on self!

    Create read_value(),
        Do skip() on self.
        if pos is Counted(text), give Do fail("unexpected end of text") on self.
        A c holds text:pos.
        if c is "{{", give Do read_object() on self.
        if c is "[", give Do read_array() on self.
        if c is "\"", give Do read_string() on self.
        if c in "tfn", give Do read_word() on self.
        give Do read_number() on self!

    Create read_member(),
        Do skip() on self.
        A key holds Do read_string() on self.
        Do expect(":") on self.
        A val holds Do read_value() on self.
        give [key, val]!

    Create read_object(),
        Book-of out.
        A done holds No.
        pos holds pos + 1.
        Do skip() on self.
        if pos is smaller-than Counted(text) and text:pos is "}", pos holds pos + 1, done holds Yes.
        for every step in range(Counted(text) - pos), if done is No and problem is "", A pair holds Do read_member() on self, if problem is "", out[pair:0] holds pair:1, A sep holds Do separator("}") on self, if sep is "}", done holds Yes.
        if done is No, give Do fail("unterminated object") on self.
        give out!

    Create read_array(),
        List-of out.
        A done holds No.
        pos holds pos + 1.
        Do skip() on self.
        if pos is smaller-than Counted(text) and text:pos is "]", pos holds pos + 1, done holds Yes.
        for every step in range(Counted(text) - pos), if done is No and problem is "", A item holds Do read_value() on self, append(out, item), A sep holds Do separator("]") on self, if sep is "]", done holds Yes.
        if done is No, give Do fail("unterminated array") on self.
        give out!

    Create read_string(),
        if pos is Counted(text) or text:pos is not "\"", give Do fail("expected a string") on self.
        pos holds pos + 1.
        buf holds "".
        ended holds No.
        for every step in range(Counted(text) - pos), Do string_step() on self.
        if ended is No, give Do fail("unterminated string") on self.
        give buf!

    Create string_step(),
        Now, takes one character, or one escape like \n, and adds what it means to the text being built.
        if ended is Yes or problem is not "", give nil.
        if pos is Counted(text), give nil.
        A c holds text:pos.
        pos holds pos + 1.
        if c is "\"", ended holds Yes, give nil.
        if c is not "\\", buf holds buf plus c, give nil.
        if pos is Counted(text), give Do fail("unterminated escape") on self.
        A e holds text:pos.
        pos holds pos + 1.
        if e is "n", buf holds buf plus "\n", give nil.
        if e is "t", buf holds buf plus "\t", give nil.
        if e is "r", buf holds buf plus "\r", give nil.
        if e is "\"", buf holds buf plus "\"", give nil.
        if e is "\\", buf holds buf plus "\\", give nil.
        if e is "/", buf holds buf plus "/", give nil.
        give Do fail("unsupported escape \\{e}") on self!

    Create read_word(),
        buf holds "".
        for every step in range(6), Do word_step() on self.
        if buf is "true", give Yes.
        if buf is "false", give No.
        if buf is "null", give nil.
        give Do fail("unexpected word") on self!

    Create word_step(),
        if pos is smaller-than Counted(text) and text:pos in "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz", buf holds buf plus text:pos, pos holds pos + 1.
        give nil!

    Create read_number(),
        buf holds "".
        for every step in range(40), Do number_step() on self.
        if buf is "", give Do fail("unexpected character") on self.
        if Do is_json_number(buf) is No, give Do fail("bad number") on self.
        give number(buf)!

    Create number_step(),
        if pos is smaller-than Counted(text) and text:pos in "0123456789+-.eE", buf holds buf plus text:pos, pos holds pos + 1.
        give nil!
!

Create parse(text),
    A p holds Do Parser(text).
    A result holds Do read_value() on p.
    Do skip() on p.
    if problem of p is "" and pos of p is not Counted(text), Do fail("extra data") on p.
    if problem of p is not "", give [No, problem of p].
    give [Yes, result]!

Create loads(text),
    A outcome holds Do parse(text).
    if outcome:0 is No, say("json error: {outcome:1}"), give nil.
    give outcome:1!
